                <pb facs="0564" n="560" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg560"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1197/1205: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bucknell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-16T10:00:00+01:00">June 16, 1938—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 17—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>130. From Fuller. Preparatory Committee has included in its report statement that
                    the American representative proposed that Convention should lay down principles
                    which would provide (1) complete independence for any control body vested by the
                    Convention with authority, (2) businesslike arrangement whereby parties accept
                    responsibility for and agree to pay through machinery set up by the Convention
                    each their fair share of cost of implementation. [Fuller.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bucknell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
